From 8feb7fac77fd1e21cc15f5f46d6ee0ce319de85d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 08:54:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: Temporal anti-aliasing stage (F-223A)

- HD.TAA at BeforeUi order 850 (before CMAA2): asks for the world jitter
  while on; resolves the jittered frame against an RGBA16F history
  reprojected by depth (one matrix: current unjittered NDC -> previous
  clip), Catmull-Rom history, YCoCg variance clipping, luma-weighted
  blend, then a neighbourhood-clamped sharpen
- hdTAA (off), hdTAABlend 0.1, hdTAASharpen 0.3, hdTAADebug (motion
  view), hdTAAInfo; shader built by shader-work/taa_spv.py

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UHcJJVC4feQ4s15e9bNRoN
